Z||000014||william_thorniii||12-15-2000||08:41 PM||||GTB,<P>You can't go wrong with BT... his live show is much better than any of his recorded tracks.  If you liked that, you will really like Mocean Worker (I spelled it wrong last time).  The Crystal Method had an excellent album a while back titled Vegas.  Their other stuff has been so-so.  One of my absolute favorite electronic albums was the Cure's All Mixed Up.  It is old scool... circa 1990.  I still listen to it often and can't tell it is dated other than the fact that the dubs are taken from older Cure songs.  You should check it out.  Also there is a cool song out called "Human Disco Ball" by the Mexican band Plastilina Mosh.  One of my all time favorites is "I am the Freshmaker" by Freshmaker... cheesy but cool/funny.<P>Also I have an addendum to your prior "chill music" post... at least I think it was yours.  You must check out Karate, Coldplay, <BR>Grandaddy, Doves and Catherine Wheel (I think I mentioned them before) Hooverphonic - saw them live too.  Not only is the lead a super hottie but they can play some serious indie/alt/modern music.  Another good single (don't know anything else about the band) is "The Way you Walk" by Papas Fritas.  Oh yeah... Cake is back together and a new CD will be released in the Spring.  <P>Give me a little help here.  I am new to downloading mp3's.  Where are you trading now that some of the biggies are gone (scour, freenet, etc.).  I know that Napster is still up but I will not want to pay the membership fee.  Any suggestions?    <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000015||onfire||12-21-2000||05:24 AM||||This looks promising william. My friend sent it to me yesturday, I haven't tried it yet. <A HREF="http://freenet.sourceforge.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://freenet.sourceforge.net/</A> <P>Their is Imesh also. Which I have used, but it kept crashing my computer. Maybe I will try again after a new version comes out. <A HREF="http://www.imesh.com/index.cfm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.imesh.com/index.cfm</A> <P>------------------<BR>"I seen it on the internet, and I believe everthing on the net."<BR><A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank>Check out my waist of banbwidth.</A><p>[This message has been edited by onfire (edited 12-21-2000).]||||reg||1
